hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27569","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from al-Khattab ibn Salih, from his mother, she said: Salamah bint Maqil narrated to me, she said: I belonged to al-Hubab ibn Amr, and I had a boy by him. His wife said to me: Now you will be sold for his debt. I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Who is the holder of the inheritance of al-Hubab ibn Amr? They said: His brother Abu al-Yusr Kab ibn Amr. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called him and said: Do not sell her, and free her; when you hear of slaves - he thought - then come to me and I will compensate you. They did so, then differed among themselves after the death of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Some said: The mother of a child is owned; had it not been that, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not have compensated them for her. And some said: She is free; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, freed her. Concerning me was the disagreement."
